ption":"Find the asterisks in the help and check how command docs are regenerated"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"31fbc029-60e9-43c8-a024-22cade8897f4","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgeB5vDoUiURjNfytAUHZ","requestRef":"b51bdbec-5f29-4447-9317-4c2ad80a3629","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d42c013c-b9df-47b9-b3b9-e17fe1b00700","timestamp":"2026-11-02T13:24:14.236Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/merill/github/maester","sessionId":"2d9f0177-c129-494c-a54f-610e3d37d77a","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"feat/website-astro","slug":"breezy-giggling-flame"}
{"parentUuid":"d42c013c-b9df-47b9-b3b9-e17fe1b00700","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"965940d5-f797-4efc-9677-e515317c5404","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JA6KxdrLNUpWpiDibSNufa","type":"tool_result","content":"11:    By default, Invoke-Maester runs the tests that ship with Maester and the custom tests in the Custom folder of the current directory, except Active Directory tests, preview tests and long-running tests. With -Path, native custom tests (Test.*.ps1) are found anywhere under the path and Pester-format custom tests (*.Tests.ps1) only in a Custom folder. Folders are searched up to three levels deep. Active Directory tests run only after an explicit Connect-Maester -Service ActiveDirectory call succeeds.\n16:    Do not run the tests of these products: keys such as entra or exchange, or an alias such as 'exo' or 'Entra ID'. Matches a test's Product or any of its RelatedProduct values, and '*' wildcards are allowed, as for -Product. Adds to Selection.ExcludeProduct in the run configuration and wins over -Product, -TestId and the other selectors. Excluded tests are reported as NotRun with the reason code ExcludedByProduct. A test without a product, such as a Pester-format custom test, is never excluded.\n147:    Invoke-Maester -TestId 'MT.1005', 'CISA.MS.AAD.3.*'\n152:    Invoke-Maester -ExcludeTestId 'MT.1024.*' -DryRun -PassThru\n577:            $urlPattern = '^(https)://[^\\s/$.?#].[^\\s]*$'\n744:                $packSelect = @($TestId | Where-Object { $_ -match '^MP\\.[^.]+\\.' } | ForEach-Object { ($_ -replace '^MP\\.', '') -replace '\\.[^.]*$', '' } | Select-Object -Unique)\n833:                    -not ($nativeAll | Where-Object { $_.Id -eq $id -or ($_.InstanceSource -and $id -like \"$($_.Id).*\") })\n1053:                    $jsonResults = $maesterResults | Select-Object -Property * -ExcludeProperty Attachments\n1054:                    $jsonResults | Add-Member -MemberType NoteProperty -Name 'Attachments' -Value @($maesterResults.Attachments | Select-Object -Property * -ExcludeProperty Content)\n11:    By default, Invoke-Maester runs the tests that ship with Maester and the custom tests in the Custom folder of the current directory, except Active Directory tests, preview tests and long-running tests. With -Path, native custom tests (Test.*.ps1) are found anywhere under the path and Pester-format custom tests (*.Tests.ps1) only in a Custom folder. Folders are searched up to three levels deep. Active Directory tests run only after an explicit Connect-Maester -Service ActiveDirectory call succeeds.\npowershell/public/run/Invoke-Maester.ps1:104:    ```powershell\npowershell/public/run/Invoke-Maester.ps1:111:    ```\npowershell/public/run/Invoke-Maester.ps1:116:    ```powershell\npowershell/public/run/Invoke-Maester.ps1:119:    ```\npowershell/public/run/Invoke-Maester.ps1:124:    ```powershell\n/usr/local/bin/pwsh\n﻿# Description: This script is used to generate the 'Command Reference' section of the Maester website (website/docs/commands)\n# * This command needs to be run from the root of the project. e.g. ./build/Build-CommandReference.ps1\n# * If the website dev server is running, restart it after running this command so it picks up the new pages\n\n# Alt3 2.x requires Microsoft.PowerShell.PlatyPS, whose YamlDotNet assembly conflicts with legacy PlatyPS.\n$alt3DocusaurusVersion = \"1.0.37\"\n$platyPSVersion = \"0.14.2\"\n\nif (-not (Get-Module Alt3.Docusaurus.Powershell -ListAvailable | Where-Object { $_.Version -eq $alt3DocusaurusVersion })) { Install-Module Alt3.Docusaurus.Powershell -RequiredVersion $alt3DocusaurusVersion -Scope CurrentUser -Force -SkipPublisherCheck }\nif (-not (Get-Module PlatyPS -ListAvailable | Where-Object { $_.Version -eq $platyPSVersion })) { Install-Module PlatyPS -RequiredVersion $platyPSVersion -Scope CurrentUser -Force -SkipPublisherCheck }\nif (-not (Get-Module Pester -ListAvailable | Where-Object { $_.Version -eq '5.7.1' })) { Install-Module Pester -RequiredVersion 5.7.1 -Scope CurrentUser -Force -SkipPublisherCheck }\n\nImport-Module Alt3.Docusaurus.Powershell -RequiredVersion $alt3DocusaurusVersion\nImport-Module PlatyPS -RequiredVersion $platyPSVersion\nImport-Module Pester -RequiredVersion 5.7.1\nImport-Module DnsClient\n\n# Generate the command reference markdown\n$commandsIndexFile = \"./website/docs/commands/readme.mdx\"\n$readmeContent = Get-Content $commandsIndexFile  # Backup the index page, since New-DocusaurusHelp replaces the folder\n\n# Exclude internal script filenames as well as any helper function names declared inside\n# internal script files so multi-function files do not leak private helpers into docs.\n# Recurse so helpers in nested folders (e.g. internal/services/ad/queries, internal/generated/eidsca) are excluded too.\n$internalCommandFiles = Get-ChildItem ./powershell/internal -Recurse -Filter *.ps1\n$internalCommands = $internalCommandFiles | ForEach-Object { $_.BaseName }\n$internalFunctionNames = foreach ($file in $internalCommandFiles) {\n    foreach ($match in [regex]::Matches((Get-Content $file.FullName -Raw), '(?m)^\\s*function\\s+([A-Za-z0-9-]+)\\s*\\{')) {\n        $match.Groups[1].Value\n    }\n}\n$commandsToExclude = ($internalCommands + $internalFunctionNames) | Sort-Object -Unique\n\n# The manifest, not the .psm1: in a source checkout the .psm1 exports every function it loads, including\n# the check functions of the native tests, which are internal in Maester 3.0. Only exported commands get a page.\nNew-DocusaurusHelp -Module ./powershell/Maester.psd1 -DocsFolder ./website/docs -NoPlaceHolderExamples -EditUrl https://github.com/maester365/maester/blob/main/powershell/public/ -Exclude $commandsToExclude\n\n# New-DocusaurusHelp only knows the flat -EditUrl root above, so every generated custom_edit_url\n# assumes commands live directly under powershell/public/. Most commands actually live in nested\n# category folders (e.g. powershell/public/services/exchange/), which produces a dead \"Edit this","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"753d1ba6-62fb-408e-9f7b-f6d926638907","timestamp":"2026-11-02T13:24:14.988Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"11:    By default, Invoke-Maester runs the tests that ship with Maester and the custom tests in the Custom folder of the current directory, except Active Directory tests, preview tests and long-running tests. With -Path, native custom tests (Test.*.ps1) are found anywhere under the path and Pester-format custom tests (*.Tests.ps1) only in a Custom folder. Folders are searched up to three levels deep. Active Directory tests run only after an explicit Connect-Maester -Service ActiveDirectory call succeeds.\n16:    Do not run the tests of these products: keys such as entra or exchange, or an alias such as 'exo' or 'Entra ID'. Matches a test's Product or any of its RelatedProduct values, and '*' wildcards are allowed, as for -Product. Adds to Selection.ExcludeProduct in the run configuration and wins over -Product, -TestId and the other selectors. Excluded tests are reported as NotRun with the reason code ExcludedByProduct. A test without a product, such as a Pester-format custom test, is never excluded.\n147:    Invoke-Maester -TestId 'MT.1005', 'CISA.MS.AAD.3.*'\n152:    Invoke-Maester -ExcludeTestId 'MT.1024.*' -DryRun -PassThru\n577:            $urlPattern = '^(https)://[^\\s/$.?#].[^\\s]*$'\n744:                $packSelect = @($TestId | Where-Object { $_ -match '^MP\\.[^.]+\\.' } | ForEach-Object { ($_ -replace '^MP\\.', '') -replace '\\.[^.]*$', '' } | Select-Object -Unique)\n833:                    -not ($nativeAll | Where-Object { $_.Id -eq $id -or ($_.InstanceSource -and $id -like \"$($_.Id).*\") })\n1053:                    $jsonResults = $maesterResults | Select-Object -Property * -ExcludeProperty Attachments\n1054:                    $jsonResults | Add-Member -MemberType NoteProperty -Name 'Attachments' -Value @($maesterResults.Attachments | Select-Object -Property * -ExcludeProperty Content)\n11:    By default, Invoke-Maester runs the tests that ship with Maester and the custom tests in the Custom folder of the current directory, except Active Directory tests, preview tests and long-running tests. With -Path, native custom tests (Test.*.ps1) are found anywhere under the path and Pester-format custom tests (*.Tests.ps1) only in a Custom folder. Folders are searched up to three levels deep. Active Directory tests run only after an explicit Connect-Maester -Service ActiveDirectory call succeeds.\npowershell/public/run/Invoke-Maester.ps1:104:    ```powershell\npowershell/public/run/Invoke-Maester.ps1:111:    ```\npowershell/public/run/Invoke-Maester.ps1:116:    ```powershell\npowershell/public/run/Invoke-Maester.ps1:119:    ```\npowershell/public/run/Invoke-Maester.ps1:124:    ```powershell\n/usr/local/bin/pwsh\n﻿# Description: This script is used to generate the 'Command Reference' section of the Maester website (website/docs/commands)\n# * This command needs to be run from the root of the project. e.g. ./build/Build-CommandReference.ps1\n# * If the website dev server is running, restart it after running this command so it picks up the new pages\n\n# Alt3 2.x requires Microsoft.PowerShell.PlatyPS, whose YamlDotNet assembly conflicts with legacy PlatyPS.\n$alt3DocusaurusVersion = \"1.0.37\"\n$platyPSVersion = \"0.14.2\"\n\nif (-not (Get-Module Alt3.Docusaurus.Powershell -ListAvailable | Where-Object { $_.Version -eq $alt3DocusaurusVersion })) { Install-Module Alt3.Docusaurus.Powershell -RequiredVersion $alt3DocusaurusVersion -Scope CurrentUser -Force -SkipPublisherCheck }\nif (-not (Get-Module PlatyPS -ListAvailable | Where-Object { $_.Version -eq $platyPSVersion })) { Install-Module PlatyPS -RequiredVersion $platyPSVersion -Scope CurrentUser -Force -SkipPublisherCheck }\nif (-not (Get-Module Pester -ListAvailable | Where-Object { $_.Version -eq '5.7.1' })) { Install-Module Pester -RequiredVersion 5.7.1 -Scope CurrentUser -Force -SkipPublisherCheck }\n\nImport-Module Alt3.Docusaurus.Powershell -RequiredVersion $alt3DocusaurusVersion\nImport-Module PlatyPS -RequiredVersion $platyPSVersion\nImport-Module Pester -RequiredVersion 5.7.1\nImport-Module DnsClient\n\n# Generate the command reference markdown\n$commandsIndexFile = \"./website/docs/commands/readme.mdx\"\n$readmeContent = Get-Content $commandsIndexFile  # Backup the index page, since New-DocusaurusHelp replaces the folder\n\n# Exclude internal script filenames as well as any helper function names declared inside\n# internal script files so multi-function files do not leak private helpers into docs.\n# Recurse so helpers in nested folders (e.g. internal/services/ad/queries, internal/generated/eidsca) are excluded too.\n$internalCommandFiles = Get-ChildItem ./powershell/internal -Recurse -Filter *.ps1\n$internalCommands = $internalCommandFiles | ForEach-Object { $_.BaseName }\n$internalFunctionNames = foreach ($file in $internalCommandFiles) {\n    foreach ($match in [regex]::Matches((Get-Content $file.FullName -Raw), '(?m)^\\s*function\\s+([A-Za-z0-9-]+)\\s*\\{')) {\n        $match.Groups[1].Value\n    }\n}\n$commandsToExclude = ($internalCommands + $internalFunctionNames) | Sort-Object -Unique\n\n# The manifest, not the .psm1: in a source checkout the .psm1 exports every function it loads, including\n# the check functions of the native tests, which are internal in Maester 3.0. Only exported commands get a page.\nNew-DocusaurusHelp -Module ./powershell/Maester.psd1 -DocsFolder ./website/docs -NoPlaceHolderExamples -EditUrl https://github.com/maester365/maester/blob/main/powershell/public/ -Exclude $commandsToExclude\n\n# New-DocusaurusHelp only knows the flat -EditUrl root above, so every generated custom_edit_url\n# assumes commands live directly under powershell/public/. Most commands actually live in nested\n# category folders (e.g. powershell/public/services/exchange/), which produces a dead \"Edit this","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpe