{"parentUuid":"cc034ec9-ba60-4f79-a486-5f082e8cb36f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgeBCkmUmzFNTVwewosxF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've fixed the help, and the stray italics on the Invoke-Maester page are gone. The two file patterns now show as code. I haven't committed anything, and I haven't run the module's unit tests (`./powershell/tests/pester.ps1`), which you should do before pushing because two module source files changed.\n\n- **The fix:** in `powershell/public/run/Invoke-Maester.ps1` I put `Test.*.ps1` and `*.Tests.ps1` in backticks, which is how other help in the module already marks inline code. I regenerated the page with `./build/Update-CommandReference.ps1` rather than editing it by hand.\n\n- **Something regenerating turned up:** `:::info` was used in two places, and Starlight has no info callout, so both show as plain text: the help in `Invoke-MtGraphRequest.ps1` and the \"Why Maester?\" box in `docs/intro.mdx`. The command page had been hand-edited to `:::note`, so regenerating it would have quietly broken it again. I changed both sources to `:::note`, and they now render as callouts.\n\n- **Checked:** after regenerating, Invoke-Maester is the only command page that changed. The build passes and all 2,679 old URLs still resolve."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_read_input_tokens":362823,"output_tokens":404,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":352,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":404,"cache_read_input_tokens":362823,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":352},"type