{"parentUuid":"8a18f5f4-b991-4095-8df2-c294de956302","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgeCLt9KoiHAHREfcVie9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is pushed to `origin/feat/website-astro` as one commit, `3a7c06795`. There's no pull request yet; GitHub's link for one is https://github.com/maester365/maester/pull/new/feat/website-astro.\n\n- **Remote branch:** the branch was set to track `origin/main`, so a plain `git push` would have gone to main. I pushed to `feat/website-astro` by name, and the branch now tracks that, so later pushes go there too.\n- **What's in it:** the whole site rebuild. That includes removing the Docusaurus files, plus the 2.x archive's command and test pages; their old URLs redirect to the current pages. The two help fixes are in it too, with their regenerated command page.\n- **Unit tests:** 6,566 of 6,567 passed. The one failure is specific to this machine. A Zero Trust Assessment test expects the ZeroTrustAssessment module to be missing, and you have version 3.1.0 installed, so it reports an error instead of skipping. This branch only changes help text in the module, so it should pass in CI.\n- **Cleanup:** my first screenshot run had left seven PNGs in `website/`; I deleted them before committing.\n\nGitHub also reported 13 Dependabot alerts on the main branch when I pushed (5 high, 6 moderate, 2 low). They're on main, not new in this commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":290,"cache_read_input_tokens":373322,"output_tokens":451,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":290,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":451,"cache_read_input_tokens":37332