{"parentUuid":"c710a1e2-77c9-4f76-a4ac-32938a2fbaf8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ea1ea568-801d-4424-a643-e8d56708832f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A77bTfkjLjk5DwQHrkX7u2","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Shown in the next-step box. Do not call wrap_up again this turn; the advice that follows is for your next call. recap is two or three sentences (about 300 characters); this one ran 311. Keep it to what is now true and where it stands. Your closing message is your answer to the user: write it now, in full, as the last thing you say this turn. The box asks your question, so do not ask it again."}]}]},"uuid":"d322522a-aca9-4756-9b4c-72f14462b621","timestamp":"2026-11-02T19:48:30.451Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"Shown in the next-step box. Do not call wrap_up again this turn; the advice that follows is for your next call. recap is two or three sentences (about 300 characters); this one ran 311. Keep it to what is now true and where it stands. Your closing message is your answer to the user: write it now, in full, as the last thing you say this turn. The box asks your question, so do not ask it again."}],"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c710a1e2-77c9-4f76-a4ac-32938a2fbaf8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"rule","ruleSource":"cliArg"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro","sessionId":"2d9f0177-c129-494c-a54f-610e3d37d77a","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"feat/website-astro","slug":"breezy-giggling-flame"}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"2d9f0177-c129-494c-a54f-610e3d37d77a","id":"1e772ac6-0fd2-46ef-bbcb-2cf7603fb427","timestamp":"2026-11-02T19:48:30.714Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"6acc74749ed5f4c81c3d8205946847d54e939575620b08685a1621bb356ac052","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"3d4dadfd-5e47-4255-a4a6-c63319b61aa3","keep":19,"tail":["11eee168977787f99a233f349889838771a25a6e00cedd51d6137b4ce7a51f9a","0a8e771b1a2718b2cc9a4fb17a683ce0930e821cf2b63de87dcdca0c68b33d91"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",20,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"e3ecbca0d30d17f339012dafaaa6aa3d861c202c67973826b1e03ef35f8172f2"}
{"parentUuid":"d322522a-aca9-4756-9b4c-72f14462b621","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgegQ4U21k994uiH9SDh1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Short answer:** yes, all three are still needed as things stand. Each one exists only because Cloudflare Pages builds from what's committed to the repo, and it can't run PowerShell or use the bot's token to call GitHub. If the site is built and deployed from GitHub Actions instead, none of the three has to open a PR.\n\n**Why they're still needed today**\n\n| Workflow | What it commits | Why it's still needed |\n|---|---|---|\n| `update-sponsors` (daily) | `src/data/sponsors.json` and the Sponsors section of `README.md` | The sponsor page reads that JSON. Finding out which people have a Sponsors listing needs GitHub's API with the bot's token. |\n| `update-module-docs` | `website/docs/commands/*.mdx` | The command pages are built from those files. Generating them needs PowerShell and PlatyPS, and the job runs on a Windows runner. |\n| `update-test-docs` | `src/data/test-catalog.json`, `contributors.json`, `email-aliases.json` | The test pages and contributor credits are built from those files. The export needs PowerShell, and the credits need the full git history. |\n\nOne thing has already changed with the new site: there are no generated test pages in git any more (`website/docs/tests` is gone). Only the JSON catalog is committed.\n\n**Why you have to merge them by hand:** the `main` ruleset requires one approving review and approval of the last push. A bot PR can never meet that on its own. Turning on auto-merge wouldn't fix it, and auto-merge is also switched off on the repo.\n\n**Options**\n\n1. **Deploy from GitHub Actions (recommended).** On every push to `main`, plus once a day for sponsors, a workflow would:\n   - export the catalog;\n   - generate the command pages;\n   - work out contributors and sponsors with the bot's token;\n   - build the site;\n   - upload it to Cloudflare with `wrangler pages deploy`.\n\n   The generated files stop being committed and get ignored by git. This removes all three PRs and the noise they add to the diffs. Most of these steps are already in `build-website.yaml`, which runs them on every PR to check the build.\n\n   The README sponsor section is the one piece that still writes to git. It could show an image the site generates (`https://maester.dev/sponsors.svg`, or similar), so the README itself never has to change.\n\n   **What you'd need to do:** add a Cloudflare API token as a repo secret and turn off Cloudflare's own builds from git. This also replaces the change to the Cloudflare Pages build settings that's already pending for this PR.\n2. **Keep the PRs but let them merge themselves.** Add the maester-bot app as a bypass actor on the ruleset, limited to these generated paths if possible, and turn on auto-merge. This is less work, but generated files keep landing in `main`, and the bypass is a security setting only you can change.\n\nIf you choose option 1, the change could go into PR #2647 or a follow-up PR. I'd also update the \"Generated content\" rule in AGENTS.md to match."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_read_input_tokens":124268,"output_tokens":1005,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":402,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1005,"cache_read_input_tokens":124268,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":402},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"1b7464a1-6a87-4b11-93ac-1aeeb0c71282","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgegQ4DPhZ8ddzg6zVrmm","requestRef":"1e772ac6-0fd2-46ef-bbcb-2cf7603fb427","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"176a4f53-0018-4dca-8b03-3ca6878a227f","timestamp":"2026-11-02T19:48:42.661Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro","sessionId":"2d9f0177-c129-494c-a54f-610e3d37d77a","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"feat/website-astro","slug":"breezy-giggling-flame"}
