{"parentUuid":"3c7e6911-0a3b-4958-9e15-8858feb45353","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"85e869c8-29fb-4e15-90c4-611f26363c9b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NGdY9czzGJMW9sSBiwTES4","type":"tool_result","content":".coderabbit.yaml:29:    - path: \"website/docs/commands/*.mdx\"\n.coderabbit.yaml:31:        These command reference files are generated by `build/Update-CommandReference.ps1`.\nAGENTS.md:36:- Generated content — regenerate, never hand-edit: `website/docs/commands/`,\nAGENTS.md:37:  `website/src/data/test-catalog.json` (the test pages are built from it),\nwebsite/astro.config.mjs:155:\t\t\t\t\t\t\tlink: '/docs/commands',\nwebsite/astro.config.mjs:184:\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcommands: ['/docs/commands/**/*'],\nwebsite/README.md:19:| `docs/` | The guides and the command reference (`docs/commands`, generated by `build/Update-CommandReference.ps1`). A file's path is its URL. |\nwebsite/README.md:22:| `src/data/test-catalog.json` | Every built-in test, exported by `npm run export-catalog`. The test pages and the catalog are built from it at build time by `scripts/generate-tes\nwebsite/docs/contributing.md:111:   `.LINK` to `https://maester.dev/docs/commands/<Name>`. The command reference page is generated from it.\nwebsite/docs/contributing.md:331:The docs/commands folder is auto-generated based on the comments in the PowerShell cmdlets. If you want to update the documentation for a command, you will need to upd\nwebsite/docs/contributing.md:374:  website. `npm run export-catalog` refreshes `website/src/data/test-catalog.json` from your local tests (it needs\nwebsite/contributors/contributors.yml:28:# email-aliases.json — a machine-maintained file, don't edit it), and your\nwebsite/contributors/README.md:21:   [`email-aliases.json`](./email-aliases.json) (machine-maintained — never\nwebsite/contributors/README.md:23:4. The result is snapshotted to `website/src/data/contributors.json` (used when CI\nwebsite/sponsors/featured.yml:4:# 