s/README.md; sed -n 24,32p website/contributors/contributors.yml; echo ----; sed -n 150,158p .github/skills/maester-triage/SKILL.md; sed -n 57,62p .github/skills/maester-test-expert/SKILL.md; sed -n 629,633p .github/skills/maester-test-expert/SKILL.md; sed -n 25,36p .coderabbit.yaml","description":"Read docs passages that mention the old flow"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_018b2Vgw2ZzcsJDaTCdF39bf":{"cwd":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1f32193f-2ac7-4925-9317-01cf46bda816","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgehGouqncX432WWRTroJ","requestRef":"f0b9ea7b-fea6-49ae-9cbb-757610528a06","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ae9eae30-f5a3-4911-95eb-5839f74a4aa1","timestamp":"2026-11-02T20:00:07.631Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro","sessionId":"2d9f0177-c129-494c-a54f-610e3d37d77a","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"feat/website-astro","slug":"breezy-giggling-flame"}
{"parentUuid":"ae9eae30-f5a3-4911-95eb-5839f74a4aa1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"85e869c8-29fb-4e15-90c4-611f26363c9b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018b2Vgw2ZzcsJDaTCdF39bf","type":"tool_result","content":"## Hard rules\n\n- Generated content — regenerate, never hand-edit: `website/docs/commands/`,\n  `website/src/data/test-catalog.json` (the test pages are built from it),\n  `website/src/data/versions.json`, `website/versioned_docs/` (the frozen 2.x docs), everything under\n  `powershell/internal/generated/`, and the native `tests/eidsca/Test.EIDSCA.*` and\n  `tests/orca/Test.ORCA.*` files the generators in `build/eidsca/` and `build/orca/`\n  write. Edit the PowerShell source, comment-based help or generator templates and let\n  automation regenerate. `powershell/assets/ConsoleContributors.json` (the dashboard's\n  Featured contributor list) is written by `./build/Update-ConsoleContributors.ps1` from\n  the website's contributor data.\n- A test is mapped to a framework in one place: the `Control` attribute, `<framework-key>:<requirement-id>`. A\n  CIS test carries `Control = 'cis-m365:5.1.5.1'`, a CISA test `Control = 'cisa-scuba:MS.AAD.3.1'`, and any other\n----\n\n## Where things are\n\n| Path | What it is |\n| --- | --- |\n| `docs/` | The guides and the command reference (`docs/commands`, generated by `build/Update-CommandReference.ps1`). A file's path is its URL. |\n| `blog/` | Blog posts, one folder each. |\n| `versioned_docs/version-2.3.0/` | The Maester 2.x docs, frozen, served at `/docs/2.x` with `noindex`. |\n| `src/data/test-catalog.json` | Every built-in test, exported by `npm run export-catalog`. The test pages and the catalog are built from it at build time by `scripts/generate-test-docs.mjs` (into the ignored `.generated/`). |\n| `src/data/versions.json` | The release each test, command and parameter first shipped in. With `version-config.js` it decides what is marked **Preview**. |\n| `src/data/url-contract.txt` | Every URL the site had before the move to Astro. The build fails if one stops resolving. |\n| `src/lib/redirects.mjs` | Writes `dist/_redirects` (Cloudflare Pages) for the URLs that moved. |\n| `src/lib/content-loader.ts` | Loads the guides, tests, 2.x archive and blog into Starlight with the URLs they had on Docusaurus. |\n| `src/components/` | Starlight overrides (`overrides/`), the version picker, the test catalog, the explainer player and the other components. |\n| `src/pages/` | The pages outside the docs: home, sponsor, contributors, manifesto, test builder, EIDSCA sync. |\n| `public/explainers/` | The HyperFrames explainers: HTML and GSAP, played live by `<Explainer>`. |\n\n----\n## Contributing to Maester docs and blog posts\n\nSimple edits can be made in the GitHub UI by selecting the `Edit this page` link at the bottom of each page or you can browse to the [docs](https://github.com/maester365/maester/tree/main/website/docs) folder on GitHub.\n\nFor more complex changes, you can fork the repository and submit a pull request.\n\nThe docs/commands folder is auto-generated based on the comments in the PowerShell cmdlets. If you want to update the documentation for a command, you will need to update the comment-based help in the .ps1 file for the command.\n\n### Running documentation locally\n\nThe [Maester.dev](https://maester.dev) website is built with [Astro](https://astro.build) and [Starlight](https://starlight.astro.build).\n- A page that uses components (tabs, icons, explainers) is an `.mdx` file and imports them, for example\n  `import { Tabs, TabItem } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';` or\n  `import IIcon from '@components/IIcon.astro';` for an [Iconify](https://icon-sets.iconify.design/) icon. See\n  [Starlight's components](https://starlight.astro.build/components/using-components/).\n- The pages under `Commands` are generated from each command's comment-based help: edit the `.ps1` file, not the page.\n- The test pages are built from each test's `[MaesterTest]` attribute and `Test.<ID>.md`: edit those, not the\n  website. `npm run export-catalog` refreshes `website/src/data/test-catalog.json` from your local tests (it needs\n  PowerShell 7 and the `Microsoft.Graph.Authentication` module).\n\n#### Stable and preview\n\nThe docs describe the preview, which is published to the PowerShell Gallery each time a change is merged. Checks,\ncommands and parameters that the stable release doesn't have are marked **Preview** automatically, from the test\n----\n   `Contributor` in the same pull request as your change.\n2. `website/scripts/contributors.mjs` reads those handles from the test catalog. Git history only fills in\n   profile details: display names and the date of a person's first contribution.\n3. Identities are matched to GitHub accounts automatically: GitHub noreply\n   addresses resolve directly; other commit emails are resolved once via the\n   GitHub API and cached as privacy-preserving hashes in\n   [`email-aliases.json`](./email-aliases.json) (machine-maintained — never\n   edit it by hand); git author names cover the rest.\n4. The result is snapshotted to `website/src/data/contributors.json` (used when CI\n   builds from a shallow clone) and rendered into the generated test docs.\n\nRun `npm run generate-test-docs` in `website/` to refresh.\n\n## Make your profile shine ✨\n\nAttribution works with zero setup, but you can enrich your profile card:\n#\n# Commit matching is fully automatic — you never need to list emails here.\n# Commits are matched to your GitHub account via your noreply email, the\n# GitHub API (results cached as privacy-preserving hashes in\n# email-aliases.json — a machine-maintained file, don't edit it), and your\n# git author name.\n#\n# Profile picture: your GitHub avatar is used by default. To use a different\n# image, drop `your-github-handle.png` (or .jpg) into website/public/img/contributors/.\n----\n\n| Label | When | Who sets it |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `needs rebase` | `mergeable` is `CONFLICTING`. Remove it when the conflict is gone. | Triage |\n| `generated` | Every changed file is generated, as in the bot PRs that refresh the test catalog. Generated files are `website/src/data/test-catalog.json`, `website/src/data/contributors.json`, `website/src/data/versions.json`, `website/docs/commands/**`, `website/versioned_docs/**`, `**/fixtures/golden/**`, `website/src/data/test-builder.json`, `packs/*/catalog.json`, the upstream-generated suites `tests/eidsca/**`, `tests/orca/**` and `powershell/internal/generated/**`, the agent and skill copies `.claude/agents/**`, `.claude/skills/**` and `website/docs/agents-and-skills.md` that `build/github/Update-AgentFiles.ps1` writes, `*.dll`, lock files, and any other file whose first lines contain both \"Generated by\" and \"Do not edit\". | Triage |\n| `breaking change` | It removes or renames a public cmdlet, parameter, output field or test ID, changes a default, removes a check from the default run, or changes what a check considers correct. Fixing a check so that it matches its documented behaviour is a `bug`, not a breaking change. On an issue: the request or the reported fix would need such a change. | Triage adds; only a maintainer removes |\n| `attribute-review-override`, `good first issue`, `help wanted` | Maintainer judgement. | Never set or remove |\n\n### Resolution (maintainers only)\n- Editing ORCA tests by hand -- `tests/orca/Test.ORCA.*` (header \"Generated by ./build/orca/Update-OrcaTests.ps1\")\n  and `powershell/internal/generated/orca/check-ORCA*.ps1` are generated. Change the generator.\n- Editing test pages on the website -- they are built from the test files by\n  `website/scripts/generate-test-docs.mjs` (via `website/src/data/test-catalog.json`), so there is no page to edit.\n- Unit tests of the module itself (`powershell/tests/`).\n\n| `Invoke-MgGraphRequest` / `Get-Mg*` | Bypasses caching | `Invoke-MtGraphRequest` |\n| Using `-Severity` or `-TestTitle` on `Add-MtTestResultDetail` | Ignored for single-result checks | Set them in the attribute |\n| Editing generated EIDSCA/ORCA files or `website/src/data/test-catalog.json` | Overwritten | Change the generator or the test files |\n| Adding the function to `FunctionsToExport` | Check functions are internal in 3.0 | Don't |\n| Missing `%TestResult%` in `-Result` with `-GraphObjects` | The object table is not inserted | Include the placeholder |\n        -Identity Default in 2.1.15), the test reads only that one. Do not suggest narrowing a test to the policies\n        users receive, or widening it to policies the audit does not read. Use the thresholds the audit names or its\n        script sets. A test fails or errors, never passes, when the audited object is not returned.\n        Before suggesting a change in scope, quote the audit step that supports it.\n    - path: \"website/docs/commands/*.mdx\"\n      instructions: |\n        These command reference files are generated by `build/Update-CommandReference.ps1`.\n        The generator sets `editUrl` from a flattened `powershell/public/` base, so the URL does not always mirror the source file's nested folder on disk.\n        Do not flag `editUrl` as incorrect solely because the corresponding PowerShell source file lives in a subdirectory such as `powershell/public/run`, `powershell/public/services/entra`, or similar.\n        Only raise an issue if the link is malformed, points outside this repository, or contradicts the generator logic.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"820f1e21-fa87-4cf9-9f76-1f1c8808d70d","timestamp":"2026-11-02T20:00:08.571Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Hard rules\n\n- Generated content — regenerate, never hand-edit: `website/docs/commands/`,\n  `website/src/data/test-catalog.json` (the test pages are built from it),\n  `website/src/data/versions.json`, `website/versioned_docs/` (the frozen 2.x docs), everything under\n  `powershell/internal/generated/`, and the native `tests/eidsca/Test.EIDSCA.*` and\n  `tests/orca/Test.ORCA.*` files the generators in `build/eidsca/` and `build/orca/`\n  write. Edit the PowerShell source, comment-based help or generator templates and let\n  automation regenerate. `powershell/assets/ConsoleContributors.json` (the dashboard's\n  Featured contributor list) is written by `./build/Update-ConsoleContributors.ps1` from\n  the website's contributor data.\n- A test is mapped to a framework in one place: the `Control` attribute, `<framework-key>:<requirement-id>`. A\n  CIS test carries `Control = 'cis-m365:5.1.5.1'`, a CISA test `Control = 'cisa-scuba:MS.AAD.3.1'`, and any other\n----\n\n## Where things are\n\n| Path | What it is |\n| --- | --- |\n| `docs/` | The guides and the command reference (`docs/commands`, generated by `build/Update-CommandReference.ps1`). A file's path is its URL. |\n| `blog/` | Blog posts, one folder each. |\n| `versioned_docs/version-2.3.0/` | The Maester 2.x docs, frozen, served at `/docs/2.x` with `noindex`. |\n| `src/data/test-catalog.json` | Every built-in test, exported by `npm run export-catalog`. The test pages and the catalog are built from it at build time by `scripts/generate-test-docs.mjs` (into the ignored `.generated/`). |\n| `src/data/versions.json` | The release each test, command and parameter first shipped in. With `version-config.js` it decides what is marked **Preview**. |\n| `src/data/url-contract.txt` | Every URL the site had before the move to Astro. The build fails if one stops resolving. |\n| `src/lib/redirects.mjs` | Writes `dist/_redirects` (Cloudflare Pages) for the URLs that moved. |\n| `src/lib/content-loader.ts` | Loads the guides, tests, 2.x archive and blog into Starlight with the URLs they had on Docusaurus. |\n| `src/components/` | Starlight overrides (`overrides/`), the version picker, the test catalog, the explainer player and the other components. |\n| `src/pages/` | The pages outside the docs: home, sponsor, contributors, manifesto, test builder, EIDSCA sync. |\n| `public/explainers/` | The HyperFrames explainers: HTML and GSAP, played live by `<Explainer>`. |\n\n----\n## Contributing to Maester docs and blog posts\n\nSimple edits can be made in the GitHub UI by selecting the `Edit this page` link at the bottom of each page or you can browse to the [docs](https://github.com/maester365/maester/tree/main/website/docs) folder on GitHub.\n\nFor more complex changes, you can fork the repository and submit a pull request.\n\nThe docs/commands folder is auto-generated based on the comments in the PowerShell cmdlets. If you want to update the documentation for a command, you will need to update the comment-based help in the .ps1 file for the command.\n\n### Running documentation locally\n\nThe [Maester.dev](https://maester.dev) website is built with [Astro](https://astro.build) and [Starlight](https://starlight.astro.build).\n- A page that uses components (tabs, icons, explainers) is an `.mdx` file and imports them, for example\n  `import { Tabs, TabItem } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';` or\n  `import IIcon from '@components/IIcon.astro';` for an [Iconify](https://icon-sets.iconify.design/) icon. See\n  [Starlight's components](https://starlight.astro.build/components/using-components/).\n- The pages under `Commands` are generated from each command's comment-based help: edit the `.ps1` file, not the page.\n- The test pages are built from each test's `[MaesterTest]` attribute and `Test.<ID>.md`: edit those, not the\n  website. `npm run export-catalog` refreshes `website/src/data/test-catalog.json` from your local tests (it needs\n  PowerShell 7 and the `Microsoft.Graph.Authentication` module).\n\n#### Stable and preview\n\nThe docs describe the preview, which is published to the PowerShell Gallery each time a change is merged. Checks,\ncommands and parameters that the stable release doesn't have are marked **Preview** automatically, from the test\n----\n   `Contributor` in the same pull request as your change.\n2. `website/scripts/contributors.mjs` reads those handles from the test catalog. Git history only fills in\n   profile details: display names and the date of a person's first contribution.\n3. Identities are matched to GitHub accounts automatically: GitHub noreply\n   addresses resolve directly; other commit emails are resolved once via the\n   GitHub API and cached as privacy-preserving hashes in\n   [`email-aliases.json`](./email-aliases.json) (machine-maintained — never\n   edit it by hand); git author names cover the rest.\n4. The result is snapshotted to `website/src/data/contributors.json` (used when CI\n   builds from a shallow clone) and rendered into the generated test docs.\n\nRun `npm run generate-test-docs` in `website/` to refresh.\n\n## Make your profile shine ✨\n\nAttribution works with zero setup, but you can enrich your profile card:\n#\n# Commit matching is fully automatic — you never need to list emails here.\n# Commits are matched to your GitHub account via your noreply email, the\n# GitHub API (results cached as privacy-preserving hashes in\n# email-aliases.json — a machine-maintained file, don't edit it), and your\n# git author name.\n#\n# Profile picture: your GitHub avatar is used by default. To use a different\n# image, drop `your-github-handle.png` (or .jpg) into website/public/img/contributors/.\n----\n\n| Label | When | Who sets it |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `needs rebase` | `mergeable` is `CONFLICTING`. Remove it when the conflict is gone. | Triage |\n| `generated` | Every changed file is generated, as in the bot PRs that refresh the test catalog. Generated files are `website/src/data/test-catalog.json`, `website/src/data/contributors.json`, `website/src/data/versions.json`, `website/docs/commands/**`, `website/versioned_docs/**`, `**/fixtures/golden/**`, `website/src/data/test-builder.json`, `packs/*/catalog.json`, the upstream-generated suites `tests/eidsca/**`, `tests/orca/**` and `powershell/internal/generated/**`, the agent and skill copies `.claude/agents/**`, `.claude/skills/**` and `website/docs/agents-and-skills.md` that `build/github/Update-AgentFiles.ps1` writes, `*.dll`, lock files, and any other file whose first lines contain both \"Generated by\" and \"Do not edit\". | Triage |\n| `breaking change` | It removes or renames a public cmdlet, parameter, output field or test ID, changes a default, removes a check from the default run, or changes what a check considers correct. Fixing a check so that it matches its documented behaviour is a `bug`, not a breaking change. On an issue: the request or the reported fix would need such a change. | Triage adds; only a maintainer removes |\n| `attribute-review-override`, `good first issue`, `help wanted` | Maintainer judgement. | Never set or remove |\n\n### Resolution (maintainers only)\n- Editing ORCA tests by hand -- `tests/orca/Test.ORCA.*` (header \"Generated by ./build/orca/Update-OrcaTests.ps1\")\n  and `powershell/internal/generated/orca/check-ORCA*.ps1` are generated. Change the generator.\n- Editing test pages on the website -- they are built from the test files by\n  `website/scripts/generate-test-docs.mjs` (via `website/src/data/test-catalog.json`), so there is no page to edit.\n- Unit tests of the module itself (`powershell/tests/`).\n\n| `Invoke-MgGraphRequest` / `Get-Mg*` | Bypasses caching | `Invoke-MtGraphRequest` |\n| Using `-Severity` or `-TestTitle` on `Add-MtTestResultDetail` | Ignored for single-result checks | Set them in the attribute |\n| Editing generated EIDSCA/ORCA files or `website/src/data/test-catalog.json` | Overwritten | Change the generator or the test files |\n| Adding the function to `FunctionsToExport` | Check functions are internal in 3.0 | Don't |\n| Missing `%TestResult%` in `-Result` with `-GraphObjects` | The object table is not inserted | Include the placeholder |\n        -Identity Default in 2.1.15), the test reads only that one. Do not suggest narrowing a test to the policies\n        users receive, or widening it to policies the audit does not read. Use the thresholds the audit names or its\n        script sets. A test fails or errors, never passes, when the audited object is not returned.\n        Before suggesting a change in scope, quote the audit step that supports it.\n    - path: \"website/docs/commands/*.mdx\"\n      instructions: |\n        These command reference files are generated by `build/Update-CommandReference.ps1`.\n        The generator sets `editUrl` from a flattened `powershell/public/` base, so the URL does not always mirror the source file's nested folder on disk.\n        Do not flag `editUrl` as incorrect solely because the corresponding PowerShell source file lives in a subdirectory such as `powershell/public/run`, `powershell/public/services/entra`, or similar.\n        Only raise an issue if the link is malformed, points outside this repository, or contradicts the generator logic.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"1f32193f-2ac7-4925-9317-01cf46bda816","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro","root":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro","branch":"feat/website-astro","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":84,"modified":12,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"maester365/maester","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"blindzero","host":"github.com","remote":"blindzero/maester","visibility":"unknown"},{"name":"jeanphilippegeorge","host":"github.com","remote":"JeanPhilippeGeorge/maester","visibility":"unknown"},{"name":"mynster","host":"github.com","remote":"Mynster9361/maester","visibility":"unknown"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"maester365/maester","visibility":"public"},{"name":"pr-author","host":"github.com","remote":"soulemike/maester","visibility":"unkn