{"parentUuid":"5cf21f2c-debd-40f5-8872-9c93e9030ec9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"85e869c8-29fb-4e15-90c4-611f26363c9b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SCp4gDGQDFhWtWipKCVFSn","type":"tool_result","content":"      instructions: |\n        A benchmark test does what the benchmark's PowerShell audit procedure does: it reads the same objects and\n        passes on the same condition (website/docs/writing-tests/index.mdx, \"What a benchmark test evaluates\").\n        Where the CIS audit reads every object (for example every Get-HostedOutboundSpamFilterPolicy result in 6.2.1),\n        the test reads every object, including ones no user receives. Where it reads one object (for example\n        -Identity Default in 2.1.15), the test reads only that one. Do not suggest narrowing a test to the policies\n        users receive, or widening it to policies the audit does not read. Use the thresholds the audit names or its\n        script sets. A test fails or errors, never passes, when the audited object is not returned.\n        Before suggesting a change in scope, quote the audit step that supports it.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"39425fb2-1ecb-441e-8343-2cb161556676","timestamp":"2026-11-02T20:00:27.483Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"      instructions: |\n        A benchmark test does what the benchmark's PowerShell audit procedure does: it reads the same objects and\n        passes on the same condition (website/docs/writing-tests/index.mdx, \"What a benchmark test evaluates\").\n        Where the CIS audit reads every object (for example every Get-HostedOutboundSpamFilterPolicy result in 6.2.1),\n        the test reads every object, including ones no user receives. Where it reads one object (for example\n        -Identity Default in 2.1.15), the test reads only that one. Do not suggest narrowing a test to the policies\n        users receive, or widening it to policies the audit does not read. Use the thresholds the audit names or its\n        script sets. A test fails or errors, never passes, when the audited object is not returned.\n        Before suggesting a change in scope, quote the audit step that supports it.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"returnCodeInterpretation":"No matches found","noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/.coderabbit.yaml","hunks":[{"oldStart":26,"oldLines":9,"newStart":26,"newLines":3,"lines":["         users receive, or widening it to policies the audit does not read. Use the thresholds the audit names or its","         script sets. A test fails or errors, never passes, when the audited object is not returned.","         Before suggesting a change in scope, quote the audit step that supports it.","-    - path: \"website/docs/commands/*.mdx\"","-      instructions: |","-        These command reference files are generated by `build/Update-CommandReference.ps1`.","-        The generator sets `editUrl` from a flattened `powershell/public/` base, so the URL does not always mirror the source file's nested folder on disk.","-        Do not flag `editUrl` as incorrect solely because the corresponding PowerShell source file lives in a subdirectory such as `powershell/public/run`, `powershell/public/services/entra`, or similar.","-        Only raise an issue if the link is malformed, points outside this repository, or contradicts the generator logic."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/.github/skills/maester-test-expert/SKILL.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":57,"oldLines":7,"newStart":57,"newLines":8,"lines":[" - Editing ORCA tests by hand -- `tests/orca/Test.ORCA.*` (header \"Generated by ./build/orca/Update-OrcaTests.ps1\")","   and `powershell/internal/generated/orca/check-ORCA*.ps1` are generated. Change the generator."," - Editing test pages on the website -- they are built from the test files by","-  `website/scripts/generate-test-docs.mjs` (via `website/src/data/test-catalog.json`), so there is no page to edit.","+  `website/scripts/generate-test-docs.mjs` (via `website/src/data/test-catalog.json`, which each build exports and","+  git doesn't keep), so there is no page to edit."," - Unit tests of the module itself (`powershell/tests/`)."," "," ## Prerequisites"]},{"oldStart":628,"oldLines":7,"newStart":629,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Multi-line `#` comment above a parameter | Only the last line is read as its description | One-line comment or `.PARAMETER` |"," | `Invoke-MgGraphRequest` / `Get-Mg*` | Bypasses caching | `Invoke-MtGraphRequest` |"," | Using `-Severity` or `-TestTitle` on `Add-MtTestResultDetail` | Ignored for single-result checks | Set them in the attribute |","-| Editing generated EIDSCA/ORCA files or `website/src/data/test-catalog.json` | Overwritten | Change the generator or the test files |","+| Editing generated EIDSCA/ORCA files | Overwritten | Change the generator or the test files |"," | Adding the function to `FunctionsToExport` | Check functions are internal in 3.0 | Don't |"," | Missing `%TestResult%` in `-Result` with `-GraphObjects` | The object table is not inserted | Include the placeholder |"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/.github/skills/maester-triage/SKILL.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":151,"oldLines":7,"newStart":151,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Label | When | Who sets it |"," | --- | --- | --- |"," | `needs rebase` | `mergeable` is `CONFLICTING`. Remove it when the conflict is gone. | Triage |","-| `generated` | Every changed file is generated, as in the bot PRs that refresh the test catalog. Generated files are `website/src/data/test-catalog.json`, `website/src/data/contributors.json`, `website/src/data/versions.json`, `website/docs/commands/**`, `website/versioned_docs/**`, `**/fixtures/golden/**`, `website/src/data/test-builder.json`, `packs/*/catalog.json`, the upstream-generated suites `tests/eidsca/**`, `tests/orca/**` and `powershell/internal/generated/**`, the agent and skill copies `.claude/agents/**`, `.claude/skills/**` and `website/docs/agents-and-skills.md` that `build/github/Update-AgentFiles.ps1` writes, `*.dll`, lock files, and any other file whose first lines contain both \"Generated by\" and \"Do not edit\". | Triage |","+| `generated` | Every changed file is generated, as in the bot PRs that mark a release on the website. Generated files are `website/src/data/versions.json`, `website/versioned_docs/**`, `**/fixtures/golden/**`, `website/src/data/test-builder.json`, `packs/*/catalog.json`, the upstream-generated suites `tests/eidsca/**`, `tests/orca/**` and `powershell/internal/generated/**`, the agent and skill copies `.claude/agents/**`, `.claude/skills/**` and `website/docs/agents-and-skills.md` that `build/github/Update-AgentFiles.ps1` writes, `*.dll`, lock files, and any other file whose first lines contain both \"Generated by\" and \"Do not edit\". | Triage |"," | `breaking change` | It removes or renames a public cmdlet, parameter, output field or test ID, changes a default, removes a check from the default run, or changes what a check considers correct. Fixing a check so that it matches its documented behaviour is a `bug`, not a breaking change. On an issue: the request or the reported fix would need such a change. | Triage adds; only a maintainer removes |"," | `attribute-review-override`, `good first issue`, `help wanted` | Maintainer judgement. | Never set or remove |"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/AGENTS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":33,"oldLines":15,"newStart":33,"newLines":18,"lines":[" "," ## Hard rules"," ","-- Generated content — regenerate, never hand-edit: `website/docs/commands/`,","-  `website/src/data/test-catalog.json` (the test pages are built from it),","-  `website/src/data/versions.json`, `website/versioned_docs/` (the frozen 2.x docs), everything under","+- Generated content — regenerate, never hand-edit: `website/src/data/versions.json`, `website/versioned_docs/` (the frozen 2.x docs), everything under","   `powershell/internal/generated/`, and the native `tests/eidsca/Test.EIDSCA.*` and","   `tests/orca/Test.ORCA.*` files the generators in `build/eidsca/` and `build/orca/`","   write. Edit the PowerShell source, comment-based help or generator templates and let","   automation regenerate. `powershell/assets/ConsoleContributors.json` (the dashboard's","   Featured contributor list) is written by `./build/Update-ConsoleContributors.ps1` from","   the website's contributor data.","+- Never commit the website data that each build generates: the command pages in `website/docs/commands/`","+  (everything but `readme.mdx`), `website/src/data/test-catalog.json`, `contributors.json` and `sponsors.json`.","+  They are ignored by git. `website/scripts/prepare-data.mjs` writes them from the module source, the git","+  history and GitHub before `npm run dev` and `npm run build`; `npm run refresh-data` writes them again.","+  The build-website workflow builds and deploys maester.dev from main, so a merge needs no follow-up PR."," - A test is mapped to a framework in one place: the `Control` attribute, `<framework-key>:<requirement-id>`. A","   CIS test carries `Control = 'cis-m365:5.1.5.1'`, a CISA test `Control = 'cisa-scuba:MS.AAD.3.1'`, and any other","   test may name the same requirements. An ASD test carries `Control = 'essential-eight:ISM-1504'` (or `ism:<id>` for a"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/website/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":16,"oldLines":10,"newStart":16,"newLines":11,"lines":[" "," | Path | What it is |"," | --- | --- |","-| `docs/` | The guides and the command reference (`docs/commands`, generated by `build/Update-CommandReference.ps1`). A file's path is its URL. |","+| `docs/` | The guides and the command reference (`docs/commands`, generated by `build/Update-CommandReference.ps1` and not kept in git). A file's path is its URL. |"," | `blog/` | Blog posts, one folder each. |"," | `versioned_docs/version-2.3.0/` | The Maester 2.x docs, frozen, served at `/docs/2.x` with `noindex`. |","-| `src/data/test-catalog.json` | Every built-in test, exported by `npm run export-catalog`. The test pages and the catalog are built from it at build time by `scripts/generate-test-docs.mjs` (into the ignored `.generated/`). |","+| `scripts/prepare-data.mjs` | Generates what the site is built from and git doesn't keep, before `npm run dev` and `npm run build`: the test catalog, the command reference, the contributor credits and the sponsors. `npm run refresh-data` generates them again. |","+| `src/data/test-catalog.json` | Every built-in test, exported from the test source (not kept in git). The test pages and the catalog are built from it at build time by `scripts/generate-test-docs.mjs` (into the ignored `.generated/`). |"," | `src/data/versions.json` | The release each test, command and parameter first shipped in. With `version-config.js` it decides what is marked **Preview**. |"," | `src/data/url-contract.txt` | Every URL the site had before the move to Astro. The build fails if one stops resolving. |"," | `src/lib/redirects.mjs` | Writes `dist/_redirects` (Cloudflare Pages) for the URLs that moved. |"]}]}],"moreFiles":3,"changedFiles":["/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/.coderabbit.yaml","/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/.github/skills/maester-test-expert/SKILL.md","/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/.github/skills/maester-triage/SKILL.md","/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/AGENTS.md","/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/website/README.md","/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/website/contributors/README.md","/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/website/docs/contributing.md","/Users/merill