{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"2d9f0177-c129-494c-a54f-610e3d37d77a","hash":"ba8fad37feee4a87a4e9aa920bdd3894a9d130cbc4a72bce3e197f9bf136a540","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SCp4gDGQDFhWtWipKCVFSn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro && python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef sub(p,a,b):\n    s=open(p).read()\n    assert a in s,(p,a[:60])\n    open(p,'w').write(s.replace(a,b))\nsub('AGENTS.md','''- Generated content — regenerate, never hand-edit: `website/docs/commands/`,\n  `website/src/data/test-catalog.json` (the test pages are built from it),\n  `website/src/data/versions.json`,''','''- Generated content — regenerate, never hand-edit: `website/src/data/versions.json`,''')\nsub('AGENTS.md','''  Featured contributor list) is written by `./build/Update-ConsoleContributors.ps1` from\n  the website's contributor data.\n''','''  Featured contributor list) is written by `./build/Update-ConsoleContributors.ps1` from\n  the website's contributor data.\n- Never commit the website data that each build generates: the command pages in `website/docs/commands/`\n  (everything but `readme.mdx`), `website/src/data/test-catalog.json`, `contributors.json` and `sponsors.json`.\n  They are ignored by git. `website/scripts/prepare-data.mjs` writes them from the module source, the git\n  history and GitHub before `npm run dev` and `npm run build`; `npm run refresh-data` writes them again.\n  The build-website workflow builds and deploys maester.dev from main, so a merge needs no follow-up PR.\n''')\nsub('website/README.md','''| `docs/` | The guides and the command reference (`docs/commands`, generated by `build/Update-CommandReference.ps1`). A file's path is its URL. |''','''| `docs/` | The guides and the command reference (`docs/commands`, generated by `build/Update-CommandReference.ps1` and not kept in git). A file's path is its URL. |''')\nsub('website/README.md','''| `src/data/test-catalog.json` | Every built-in test, exported by `npm run export-catalog`. The test pages and the catalog are built from it at build time by `scripts/generate-test-docs.mjs` (into the ignored `.generated/`). |''','''| `scripts/prepare-data.mjs` | Generates what the site is built from and git doesn't keep, before `npm run dev` and `npm run build`: the test catalog, the command reference, the contributor credits and the sponsors. `npm run refresh-data` generates them again. |\n| `src/data/test-catalog.json` | Every built-in test, exported from the test source (not kept in git). The test pages and the catalog are built from it at build time by `scripts/generate-test-docs.mjs` (into the ignored `.generated/`). |''')\nsub('website/docs/contributing.md','''- The test pages are built from each test's `[MaesterTest]` attribute and `Test.<ID>.md`: edit those, not the\n  website. `npm run export-catalog` refreshes `website/src/data/test-catalog.json` from your local tests (it needs\n  PowerShell 7 and the `Microsoft.Graph.Authentication` module).''','''- The test pages are built from each test's `[MaesterTest]` attribute and `Test.<ID>.md`: edit those, not the\n  website.\n- The first `npm start` or `npm run build` generates the test catalog and the command pages from your local\n  source, which needs PowerShell 7 and the `Microsoft.Graph.Authentication` module. After changing a test or a\n  command's help, run `npm run refresh-data` to see the change. These files aren't committed: maester.dev is built\n  from the source each time a change is merged.''')\nsub('website/contributors/README.md','''4. The result is snapshotted to `website/src/data/contributors.json` (used when CI\n   builds from a shallow clone) and rendered into the generated test docs.\n\nRun `npm run generate-test-docs` in `website/` to refresh.''','''4. The result is written to `website/src/data/contributors.json` (not kept in\n   git) and rendered into the generated test docs. Each deploy of maester.dev\n   works it out again from the full history. A profile page, once published,\n   stays: people listed in `website/src/data/url-contract.txt` keep theirs.\n\nRun `npm run refresh-data` in `website/` to refresh.''')\nsub('website/contributors/README.md','''   [`email-aliases.json`](./email-aliases.json) (machine-maintained — never\n   edit it by hand)''','''   [`email-aliases.json`](./email-aliases.json) (written by\n   `node scripts/generate-test-docs.mjs --update-aliases`, never by hand;\n   emails not in it are looked up on each build)''')\nsub('website/sponsors/featured.yml','''# Kept by hand. website/scripts/sponsors.mjs copies this list into website/src/data/sponsors.json, which the\n# page reads, and writes the README section from the same data. After editing it, run the script (no token\n# needed: `cd website && node scripts/sponsors.mjs`) or let the update-sponsors workflow do it.''','''# Kept by hand. website/scripts/sponsors.mjs copies this list into the sponsor data the page reads on each\n# build. After editing it, update the README's Sponsors section in the same pull request (no token needed:\n# `cd website && node scripts/sponsors.mjs --readme`); the build-website workflow fails until you do.''')\nsub('.github/skills/maester-triage/SKILL.md','''| `generated` | Every changed file is generated, as in the bot PRs that refresh the test catalog. Generated files are `website/src/data/test-catalog.json`, `website/src/data/contributors.json`, `website/src/data/versions.json`, `website/docs/commands/**`, `website/versioned_docs/**`,''','''| `generated` | Every changed file is generated, as in the bot PRs that mark a release on the website. Generated files are `website/src/data/versions.json`, `website/versioned_docs/**`,''')\nsub('.github/skills/maester-test-expert/SKILL.md','''`website/scripts/generate-test-docs.mjs` (via `website/src/data/test-catalog.json`), so there is no page to edit.''','''`website/scripts/generate-test-docs.mjs` (via `website/src/data/test-catalog.json`, which each build exports and\n  git doesn't keep), so there is no page to edit.''')\nsub('.github/skills/maester-test-expert/SKILL.md','''| Editing generated EIDSCA/ORCA files or `website/src/data/test-catalog.json` | Overwritten | Change the generator or the test files |''','''| Editing generated EIDSCA/ORCA files | Overwritten | Change the generator or the test files |''')\ns=open('.coderabbit.yaml').read()\ni=s.index('    - path: \"website/docs/commands/*.mdx\"')\nj=s.index('contradicts the generator logic.',i)+len('contradicts the generator logic.\\n')\nopen('.coderabbit.yaml','w').write(s[:i]+s[j:])\nEOF\nsed -n 20,30p .coderabbit.yaml; grep -n \"generate-test-docs\\\"\" website/package.json","description":"Update docs, skills and review config"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
