{"parentUuid":"2031bd2c-986a-4616-bca6-a09a9ac4b022","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgehMr4hmg9heUqHLShF1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QVxZeEfhoEVNqLobaC4ANj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add -A .github .gitignore AGENTS.md README.md .coderabbit.yaml build/Update-CommandReference.ps1 website/package.json website/scripts website/src/pages website/README.md website/docs/contributing.md website/contributors/README.md website/sponsors/featured.yml && git status --short | grep -v \"^D  website/docs/commands\" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nci(website): build maester.dev from source and deploy it from Actions\n\nThe site's generated data is no longer committed: the test catalog, the command\nreference, the contributor credits and the sponsors are written before each dev\nserver and build by website/scripts/prepare-data.mjs, and ignored by git.\n\nbuild-website.yaml now also deploys to Cloudflare Pages on every push to main,\ndaily (new sponsors) and on request. It replaces update-sponsors, update-module-docs\nand update-test-docs, which opened a pull request after each merge that had to be\napproved and merged by hand.\n\n- The README's Sponsors section shows a wall of sponsors built on each deploy\n  (maester.dev/readme/sponsors.svg), so it changes only when featured.yml does;\n  pull requests fail if it is out of date.\n- sponsors.mjs falls back to the list the last deploy published\n  (maester.dev/data/sponsors.json) without a token or when GitHub can't be read.\n- Contributor profile pages are kept by the URL contract instead of the\n  previously committed credits.\n- The release workflows credit contributors before building the module, for the\n  dashboard's Featured contributors, and no longer commit the catalog.\n- The command reference is generated on Linux (DnsClient is imported on Windows only).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit 