{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"2d9f0177-c129-494c-a54f-610e3d37d77a","id":"0f59b2f2-60b1-4eaa-998b-579dd638bdef","timestamp":"2026-11-02T20:01:53.850Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"6acc74749ed5f4c81c3d8205946847d54e939575620b08685a1621bb356ac052","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"049d7397-075c-4d2c-845b-88131286d1ed","keep":135,"tail":["12ee1cdbb514ddae7e705c30de0e03567137068e810df70d289de7c1de7d660b","97038054ca4872d541d4b64400e5864ec54acb3dee1faf8c2db8096c0e37b6d4"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",136,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"e941f8704a910c8b5ff5ff2b5065ca9ef2dbf230c6e792d0626edb3455eafede"}
{"parentUuid":"3b9667d9-56ee-4d59-8929-2aaec6a68505","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgehRGF64MD1hd7PZHf5T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The site now builds its own data on every deploy, so the sponsor, command-docs and test-docs PRs won't be opened any more. I pushed the change to PR #2647 as `7bc62f290`.\n\n**What changed**\n- **The three workflows are deleted.** `build-website.yaml` still only builds on pull requests. It now also deploys to Cloudflare Pages on every push to main, once a day (to pick up new sponsors), and when run by hand.\n- **The generated files are no longer committed.** These are the test catalog, the command pages, the contributor credits and the sponsor list. A new script, `website/scripts/prepare-data.mjs`, creates them before `npm run dev` and `npm run build`, but only when they're missing, so restarts stay fast. Run `npm run refresh-data` to regenerate them after you change a test or a command's help.\n- **The README now shows sponsors as an image** (`maester.dev/readme/sponsors.svg`) that's rebuilt on each deploy. The README itself only changes when you edit `featured.yml`. A PR that edits it without updating the README fails the build.\n- **Sponsors have a fallback.** If the GitHub lookup fails, or there's no token (as in local builds), the build uses the list the last deploy published at `maester.dev/data/sponsors.json`.\n- **The release workflows still work.** They now generate the contributor credits before building the module, so the dashboard's Featured contributors stay current. They no longer commit the catalog.\n\n**What I tested**\n- I deleted all the generated files and ran `npm run build`: it passes, and all 2,679 old URLs still resolve.\n- The regenerated command pages, the 891-test catalog and the contributor credits match the committed versions exactly.\n- The affected unit tests pass (31 of 31).\n- The workflows themselves haven't run yet: the deploy job and the PR check on the README will first run in CI.\n\n**Two side effects:**\n- Old contributor profile pages used to stay up because the build read the previously committed credits. They now stay up because their URLs are in the site's list of old URLs.\n- New contributor emails are no longer saved to `email-aliases.json`. Each build looks them up on GitHub again, which takes a few extra API calls.\n\n**What you need to set up before merging**\n1. Create a repository environment named `maester.dev` with two secrets:\n   - `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`, with the Cloudflare Pages: Edit permission;\n   - `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`.\n2. If the Cloudflare Pages project isn't named `maester`, set the repository variable `CLOUDFLARE_PAGES_PROJECT` to its name.\n3. Turn off the Cloudflare project's own builds from git. This replaces the \"output `website/dist`, Node 24\" setting change mentioned earlier.\n\nPR previews are a separate matter: Cloudflare used to build one for each PR from git. With that off, PRs are only build-checked unless we add preview deploys.\n\nOne bot PR will still need your approval: the release workflow's \"update website release version\" PR, opened once per release. It changes `versions.json`, which has to be committed. The `main` ruleset requires an approving review, so the bot can't merge it alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":221,"cache_read_input_tokens":212103,"output_tokens":1074,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":221,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1074,"cache_read_input_tokens":212103,"cache_creation_input_tokens":221,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":221},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"69143813-c315-470b-8830-c16a98cd81be","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgehRFxUPmaEUjh9xHMJm","requestRef":"0f59b2f2-60b1-4eaa-998b-579dd638bdef","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"f0418ab0-e34b-45cd-9830-a8f51faf14b9","timestamp":"2026-11-02T20:02:04.520Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro","sessionId":"2d9f0177-c129-494c-a54f-610e3d37d77a","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"feat/website-astro","slug":"breezy-giggling-flame"}
