{"parentUuid":"ae1eb66c-5c19-4ab0-ab1c-68958d97138b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgeoz9gp6NtrdkktzbGEe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EJBzvxtHo6wnw3MAznAWZa","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/api/get-started/account-owned-tokens/","prompt":"What are account-owned API tokens, how to create them (dashboard steps), limitations, which services/permissions are not supported (is Pages / Workers supported?), and can resources be restricted to a specific project?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1116,"cache_read_input_tokens":113882,"output_tokens":229,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":60},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1116,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":113882,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1116,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1116},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01EJBzvxtHo6wnw3MAznAWZa":{"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/api/get-started/account-owned-tokens/","prompt":"What are account-owned API tokens, how to create them (dashboard steps), limitations, which services/permissions are not supported (is Pages / Workers supported?), and can resources be restricted to a specific project?"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2f738e80-7a83-47d9-94ba-562ee5b7bbce","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgeoz9SgQRwBp68owkAWR","requestRef":"fbd38b46-34ec-45f0-bde9-f154135c7588","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5e692f9f-e337-4603-884f-0d3dcbc9d2e2","timestamp":"2026-11-02T21:28:04.515Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/website","sessionId":"2d9f0177-c129-494c-a54f-610e3d37d77a","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"feat/website-astro","slug":"breezy-giggling-flame"}
{"parentUuid":"5e692f9f-e337-4603-884f-0d3dcbc9d2e2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5ad2ab44-2db1-4be2-b759-d2b7d87fff40","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EJBzvxtHo6wnw3MAznAWZa","type":"tool_result","content":"**What they are:** Account API tokens are durable, service-principal-style tokens with their own permissions. They suit long-lived integrations like CI/CD or SIEM connectors that should keep working after the configuring user leaves. User tokens act for a specific user and suit ad hoc scripting. New account tokens use the `cfat_` prefix.\n\n**Creating one in the dashboard:**\n1. Log in to the Cloudflare dashboard and select your account.\n2. Go to **Manage account** > **Account API tokens**.\n3. Select **Create Token**, then enter a name, permissions, and an optional expiration date.\n4. Select **Continue to summary** and review the details.\n5. Select **Create Token**.\n\nYou need API Token Provisioning capabilities or Super Administrator status to create them. The page also notes a token can be created through the account API token creation API.\n\n**Limitations:**\n- Members can only grant permissions that are a subset of their own account permissions.\n- Super Administrators can view and manage all account API tokens in the account. Other members can only view and manage tokens they created.\n- Not every service supports them. Per the compatibility matrix, these show ❌: Intel Data Platform, Page Rules, Registrar, Super Bot Fight Mode, Turnstile, and Zero Trust Client Platform.\n\n**Pages and Workers:** Both are supported (✅). Workers KV, Workers AI, Workers Queues, and Workflows are also listed as supported.\n\n**Restricting to a specific project:** The page doesn't say whether a token can be scoped to a specific project, so I can't confirm that from this content."}]},"uuid":"ecd12a7f-da59-4821-964a-deea8276bb80","timestamp":"2026-11-02T21:28:09.664Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":6213,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**What they are:** Account API tokens are durable, service-principal-style tokens with their own permissions. They suit long-lived integrations like CI/CD or SIEM connectors that should keep working after the configuring user leaves. User tokens act for a specific user and suit ad hoc scripting. New account tokens use the `cfat_` prefix.\n\n**Creating one in the dashboard:**\n1. Log in to the Cloudflare dashboard and select your account.\n2. Go to **Manage account** > **Account API tokens**.\n3. Select **Create Token**, then enter a name, permissions, and an optional expiration date.\n4. Select **Continue to summary** and review the details.\n5. Select **Create Token**.\n\nYou need API Token Provisioning capabilities or Super Administrator status to create them. The page also notes a token can be created through the account API token creation API.\n\n**Limitations:**\n- Members can only grant permissions that are a subset of their own account permissions.\n- Super Administrators can view and manage all account API tokens in the account. Other members can only view and manage tokens they created.\n- Not every service supports them. Per the compatibility matrix, these show ❌: Intel Data Platform, Page Rules, Registrar, Super Bot Fight Mode, Turnstile, and Zero Trust Client Platform.\n\n**Pages and Workers:** Both are supported (✅). Workers KV, Workers AI, Workers Queues, and Workflows are also listed as supported.\n\n**Restricting to a specific project:** The page doesn't say whether a token can be scoped to a specific project, so I can't confirm that from this content.","durationMs":4976,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/api/get-started/account-owned-tokens/"},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2f738e80-7a83-47d9-94ba-562ee5b7bbce","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/website","root":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro","branch":"feat/website-astro","default_br