{"parentUuid":"ecd12a7f-da59-4821-964a-deea8276bb80","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgeozoEnDKtDh8Gg494t6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":757,"cache_read_input_tokens":114998,"output_tokens":1360,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":59},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":757,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1360,"cache_read_input_tokens":114998,"cache_creation_input_tokens":757,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":757},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7021,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"37f75b8a-5583-46e9-880a-f718cf024358","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgeoznxuPMDJFgyXbyhax","requestRef":"ede22dd3-540f-424f-85b1-956a4acf5bf1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"77dc471e-7d5e-4aa5-aab6-59830bb1c69d","timestamp":"2026-11-02T21:28:18.940Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/website","sessionId":"2d9f0177-c129-494c-a54f-610e3d37d77a","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"feat/website-astro","slug":"breezy-giggling-flame"}
{"parentUuid":"77dc471e-7d5e-4aa5-aab6-59830bb1c69d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgeozoEnDKtDh8Gg494t6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, use an account API token. It's owned by the Cloudflare account, not by your login, so the deploy keeps working if your user account changes or leaves the account. Cloudflare recommends account tokens for CI/CD, and they support Pages.\n\nIt doesn't restrict access to this one project, though. I found no official way to limit a token to a single Pages project. The Pages permission covers every Pages project in the account. The narrowest token you can make has only \"Cloudflare Pages: Edit\", for this account only, with an expiry date. If maester.dev must be fully isolated, put the Pages project in its own Cloudflare account.\n\n**1. Create the token in Cloudflare**\n1. In the dashboard, select the account that holds the maester.dev Pages project.\n2. Go to **Manage account → Account API tokens → Create Token → Create Custom Token**. You need Super Administrator or API Token Provisioning rights.\n3. Name it `github-actions-maester-pages`.\n4. Under **Permissions**, add one row: **Account → Cloudflare Pages → Edit**. Add nothing else; wrangler doesn't need a DNS or Workers permission for `pages deploy`.\n5. **Client IP filtering**: leave it empty. GitHub-hosted runners don't have fixed IP addresses.\n6. **TTL**: set an end date, for example 12 months, and put a reminder in your calendar to rotate it.\n7. Select **Continue to summary → Create Token**, then copy the token. It starts with `cfat_` and is shown only once.\n\n**2. Find the account ID and project name**\n- The account ID is on the account's home page. You can also copy it from the dashboard URL: `dash.cloudflare.com/<account-id>/...`.\n- Open **Workers & Pages** and note the Pages project's exact name. The workflow assumes `maester`.\n\n**3. Add them to GitHub** (maester365/maester → Settings)\n1. Go to **Environments → New environment** and name it `maester.dev`. The name must match the workflow exactly.\n2. Under **Deployment branches and tags**, choose **Selected branches** and add `main`. Then a workflow run from another branch can't read the secret.\n3. Add two environment secrets:\n   - `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`: the token.\n   - `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID`: the account ID.\n4. Only if the project isn't named `maester`: under **Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Variables**, add `CLOUDFLARE_PAGES_PROJECT` with the project name.\n5. Optional: add yourself as a **Required reviewer** on the environment if you want to approve each deploy. With the daily run, you'd be approving one every day.\n\n**4. Stop Cloudflare's own builds from git**\nIn **Workers & Pages → (project) → Settings → Builds**, disconnect the Git repository, or turn off automatic deployments for production and preview branches. Do this when you merge PR #2647. If you do it before, the site stops updating until the new workflow is on main. If you skip it, Cloudflare's own build will fail, because the generated data is no longer committed.\n\n**5. Check it after merging**\nRun **Actions → 🏗️ Build Website → Run workflow** on `main`. The deploy job should end with a URL ending in `pages.dev`, and the live site should update.\n\nTo rotate the token later: create a new one, replace the `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` secret, run the workflow once, then delete the old token.\n\nSources:\n- [Cloudflare docs: Account API tokens](https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/api/get-started/account-owned-tokens/)\n- [Cloudflare docs: Pages API](https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/api)\n- [pages-action (token setup example)](https://github.com/WhatACotton/pages-action)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":757,"cache_read_input_tokens":114998,"output_tokens":1360,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":59},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":757,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1360,"cache_read_input_tokens":114998,"cache_creation_input_tokens":757,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":757},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"37f75b8a-5583-46e9-880a-f718cf024358","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgeoznxuPMDJFgyXbyhax","requestRef":"ede22dd3-540f-424f-85b1-956a4acf5bf1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7d36a794-1748-4332-928f-3c65423fdc64","timestamp":"2026-11-02T21:28:24.248Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/merill/github/maester/.claude/worktrees/website-astro/website","sessionId":"2d9f0177-c129-494c-a54f-610e3d37d77a","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"feat/website-astro","slug":"breezy-giggling-flame"}
